---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro"
import InstallCommand from "../components/InstallCommand.astro"
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro"
import { install, releases, repo, docs } from "../data/site"
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Install"
  path="/install"
  description="Install CyxCode, connect your model provider, and start working in your repository. Setup for macOS, Linux, and Windows."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">From your terminal, forward</p><h1>Your next coding<br />environment starts here.</h1><p
      class="lead"
    >
      Install CyxCode, connect a model, and open a project. Bring your own provider credentials or configure a local
      model.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="setup" aria-label="Installation steps">
    <article class="setup-step">
      <div class="step-number">01</div><div>
        <p class="kicker">Install</p><h2>One command. Your terminal.</h2><p class="step-copy">
          Run in a shell on macOS, Linux, or Windows with WSL / Git Bash.
        </p><InstallCommand command={install} /><p class="hint">
          Installs the latest release into <code>~/.opencode/bin</code>. The compatibility path is intentional.
        </p><div class="windows-note">
          <h3>Using Windows PowerShell?</h3><p>
            Download the Windows archive from <a href={`${releases}/latest`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"
              >GitHub Releases ↗</a
            >, extract it, and run <code>cyxcode.exe</code>. Choose a build compatible with your machine.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="setup-step" id="models">
      <div class="step-number">02</div><div>
        <p class="kicker">Connect</p><h2>Your model, connected.</h2><p class="step-copy">
          Launch <code>cyxcode</code> in your project. Run <code>/connect</code> to add a provider, then <code
            >/models</code
          > to select a model.
        </p><div class="connection-grid">
          <div class="panel">
            <h3>Hosted providers</h3><p>
              Use your own credentials for a supported provider. Model access and usage charges depend on that provider
              and your account.
            </p>
          </div><div class="panel">
            <h3>Local models</h3><p>
              Configure an OpenAI-compatible local endpoint, such as Ollama, to run a model on your own hardware.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div><details class="provider-note">
          <summary>What about free models and OpenCode Zen?</summary><p>
            CyxCode's anonymous requests to OpenCode Zen have been rejected by the service. A fork of the client does
            not automatically receive access to its hosted free tier.
          </p><p>
            Connect Zen with your own API key to check your account's access. Authenticated access to Zen's free models
            has not been verified in CyxCode. Other providers may offer free models under their own limits; local models
            use your own hardware.
          </p><a
            class="text-link"
            href={`${repo}/blob/dev/README.md#providers-and-free-models`}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer noopener">Provider setup and model testing ↗</a>
        </details>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="setup-step">
      <div class="step-number">03</div><div>
        <p class="kicker">Build</p><h2>Give your project a starting point.</h2><p class="step-copy">
          Run <code>/cyxinit</code> inside CyxCode to create the project state structure. Then start with a small, concrete
          task.
        </p><div class="first-prompt">
          <span>TRY YOUR FIRST PROMPT</span><p>
            Read this project's README and explain its structure. Don't modify any files yet.
          </p>
        </div><p class="hint">
          Save conventions with <code>/remember</code>. Review captured fixes with <code>/learn-patterns</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="content-band">
    <SectionHeading kicker="Keep it yours" title="Update or build from source." /><div class="connection-grid">
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Already using CyxCode?</h3><p>
          Run <code>/update</code> inside CyxCode to check for a release. For older installs with a broken update URL, rerun
          the installer above.
        </p><a class="text-link" href={releases} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"
          >Release notes and binaries ↗</a>
      </article><article class="panel">
        <h3>Prefer to work from source?</h3><p>
          Clone the repository, install dependencies with Bun, and start the development runtime.
        </p><InstallCommand
          command={"git clone https://github.com/code3hr/cyxcode.git\ncd cyxcode\nbun install\nbun run dev"}
        />
      </article>
    </div><a class="text-link" href={docs} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Read the full documentation ↗</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page-hero {
    max-width: 780px;
  }
  .lead {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .setup {
    display: grid;
    gap: 55px;
    max-width: 960px;
  }
  .setup-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 65px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 25px;
    padding-top: 35px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    scroll-margin-top: 100px;
  }
  .step-number {
    font: 17px var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--faint);
    padding-top: 5px;
  }
  .step-copy {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 20px 0 23px;
  }
  .hint {
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin-top: 15px;
    color: var(--faint);
  }
  code {
    color: var(--mint);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  .windows-note {
    border-left: 2px solid #546e59;
    padding-left: 19px;
    margin-top: 25px;
  }
  .windows-note h3 {
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .windows-note p {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .windows-note a {
    color: var(--mint);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .connection-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .connection-grid h3 {
    font-size: 17px;
  }
  .connection-grid p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 14px 0 20px;
  }
  .provider-note {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  summary {
    font-size: 14px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .provider-note p {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin-top: 15px;
  }
  .provider-note a {
    margin-top: 17px;
  }
  .first-prompt {
    border: 1px solid #435b49;
    background: var(--mint-soft);
    padding: 22px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .first-prompt span {
    color: var(--mint);
    font: 9px var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }
  .first-prompt p {
    font: 13px/1.85 var(--font-mono);
    margin-top: 15px;
    color: #d1dfd4;
  }
  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .setup-step {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 15px;
    }
    .connection-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
